{
  "_file": {
    "path": "src/tabs/remap_fc/reference_designs.json",
    "description": "Usage -> pin/function entries for each Rotorflight reference FC design (F7A/F7B/F7C), extracted from the MCU Pin Allocation table published at github.com/rotorflight/rotorflight-ref-design. Each entry keeps the Function column (e.g. \"TX3 / SCL2 / T2CH3\") alongside its pin, so a multi-pin usage like \"Port C\" still shows which physical pin is TX vs RX (or SCL vs SDA). Looked up by the design family in FC.CONFIG.boardDesign (e.g. \"F7A1\" -> \"F7A\") to show a board-design-aware pin reference alongside the read hardware. F7A's PA3 is named \"SBUS\" here rather than \"TLM\" (as the upstream MCU Pin Allocation table calls it) -- F7A only has this one pin doing double duty as either an ESC-telemetry return or a one-wire receiver input, and the same upstream doc's own Servo and Motor Port table calls it \"SBUS\", matching what a real RadioMaster NEXUS actually silkscreens there. F7B/F7C have separate, unambiguous TLM and SBUS pins and are untouched. This file is overwritten wholesale by reference_design_source.js's live GitHub fetch of this same file from rotorflight/rotorflight-configurator's own devel branch, so it only ever holds Rotorflight's own official reference designs -- a manufacturer's own custom pin layout with no reference design behind it at all belongs in manufacturer_designs.json instead, a separate, purely local file this live fetch never touches."
